  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"1.12.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: pv\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://ivarch.com/s/pv-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 31fdbdb449c7143cd2968567bef7599e9f031950e6158ee7bb76e40aebf6ffb8\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip: win\n  script:\n    content:\n      - ./configure --prefix=\"${PREFIX}\" --build=\"${BUILD}\" --host=\"${HOST}\" --disable-dependency-tracking\n      - make -j\"${CPU_COUNT}\"\n      - if: build_platform == target_platform\n        then:\n          # Exclude Display_-_--numeric_--timer.test: uniquely among the\n          # timing tests it requires display updates spread over >=6 distinct\n          # 0.1s buckets, which fails persistently on virtualised CI runners\n          # due to timer coalescing (seen 4/4 on Azure osx-arm64).\n          # recheck absorbs the remaining timing flakes.\n          - make check TESTS=\"$(ls tests/*.test | grep -v 'numeric_--timer')\" || make recheck || make recheck\n      - make install\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - make\n    - gettext-tools\n  host:\n    - if: osx\n      then: libintl-devel\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - pv --version\n      - echo hello world | pv -q | grep hello\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - pv\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://www.ivarch.com/programs/pv.shtml\n  repository: https://codeberg.org/ivarch/pv\n  documentation: https://www.ivarch.com/programs/quickref/pv.shtml\n  license: GPL-3.0-or-later\n  license_file: docs/COPYING\n  summary: Monitor the progress of data through a pipe\n  description: |\n    pv (Pipe Viewer) is a terminal-based tool for monitoring the progress of\n    data through a pipeline and modifying its flow. It displays how quickly\n    data is being transferred, how long it has taken, how near to completion\n    it is, and an estimate of how long it will be until completion.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - shahin\n    - dbast\n",
